  "_comment": "Colour catalogue of the player identity. Every entry has a stable 'id' (stored in a save), a translated 'name' ({ fr, en }), a colour and three independent prices in Sparks: 'titlePrice' for the title line of the profile card, 'usernamePrice' for the player pseudo and 'borderPrice' for the frame of the card. A colour is either a single 'hex' string or a LIST of hex strings, which paints a gradient; 'direction' is then the angle of that gradient in degrees (null or absent means 90, left to right). A gradient entry with no valid list falls back to its first colour. The order of the list is the order of the pickers. A malformed entry is ignored rather than sold with guessed values; the shipped catalogue is used when the whole file is unreadable.",
